### Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive

- **Positive pages**: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and **Request this exact car**; the checks refuse copy that says "not available", "we don''t have" or "we don''t offer".
- **Popular cars**: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says **Popular** with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.
- **Car figures**: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer''s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer''s colours, prices and equipment.
- **Parking**: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).
- **Events**: **Marketing** > **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.
- **Turo searches**: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.
- **GPS tracker**: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).
- **Airports**: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.
- **Renting vs owning**: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.
- **Languages**: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).
- **Reviews**: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. **Reviews** > **Add a customer review** enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer''s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.
- **Sitemaps**: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page''s languages), each with its own dates.

> Good to know: The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site&#39;s own checks and published by themselves (the website&#39;s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.</p><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-copy-of-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The copy of a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car&#39;s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what&#39;s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To change a field press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and lock</b>. A locked field is kept by every new version. <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> lets it be written again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car&#39;s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car&#39;s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-landing-pages-and-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Landing pages and guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. <b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: <b class="gd-ui">Index the place pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the colour pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the search term pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the /buy pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the detailing pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the body shop pages</b>. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Financing disclaimer</b>: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People &gt; Renters, the Leads tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. <b class="gd-ui">Add trims for another model</b> adds a model that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Catalog import: the last import and its counts. <b class="gd-ui">Import now</b> asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car&#39;s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-stock-photos-on-the-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stock photos on the vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: &quot;Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons&quot;. The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet&#39;s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked &quot;not the exact year&quot;; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b>. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pick again</b> asks for the next best photo; <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show stock photos</b> in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer&#39;s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: every province, state and territory is on. Untick a region to take its pages and sitemaps off the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term (its pages then leave search), switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-alternative-searches" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alternative searches</h2><p class="gd-p">People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting (&quot;Turo Alternative in Mississauga&quot;), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages say plainly that CarmaCars does not sell, finance or lease cars; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. CarmaCars does not do this work, and the pages say so: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-what-search-engines-may-read" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What search engines may read</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Search scope</b> says what search engines are invited to read:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Full (every page)</b>, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website&#39;s CPU time as crawlers read them.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Core (about 23,000 pages)</b>: the fixed pages, the fleet&#39;s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month&#39;s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all (&quot;try again tomorrow&quot;) until the month resets. People always get every page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-indexnow" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">IndexNow</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b>, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Index coverage</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Index coverage (Search Console sample)</b> shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Longer pages from real data</h3><p class="gd-p">Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR&#39;s tolls, the city&#39;s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car&#39;s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on &quot;Crawled - currently not indexed&quot; (Indexing &gt; Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Positive pages</b>: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and <b class="gd-ui">Request this exact car</b>; the checks refuse copy that says &quot;not available&quot;, &quot;we don&#39;t have&quot; or &quot;we don&#39;t offer&quot;.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Popular cars</b>: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says <b class="gd-ui">Popular</b> with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Car figures</b>: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer&#39;s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer&#39;s colours, prices and equipment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Parking</b>: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Events</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Event pages</b> lists the Toronto and GTA events with a &quot;Rent a car for&quot; page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Turo searches</b>: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">GPS tracker</b>: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports</b>: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Renting vs owning</b>: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Languages</b>: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer&#39;s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Sitemaps</b>: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page&#39;s languages), each with its own dates.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'customer-service', 'chapter', 'your-workday', 'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Press **Adjust the booking** to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then **Save changes**.
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Save and send the update** or **Save without telling the renter**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

> Good to know: A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, **Regular** or **Troubled** (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.

## Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)

Open **Owners** (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.
2. **Onboarding photos**: **Replace** or **Remove** (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter, or **Approve** or mark it **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.
3. **Government forms**: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.
4. **Add cars from a list of VINs** for the owner: paste or upload, **Preview**, **Add**.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## Rental agreements are signed online only

A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back''s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

> Good to know: Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver''s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.

## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## Switch a booking between card coverage and the Protection Plan (release 35)

When a renter''s card does not cover the car, or they want the plan instead, switch the booking yourself. On the booking page, open the **Coverage** card.

1. Press **Switch to the Protection Plan**. You see the plan''s price with HST and the new total before you confirm.
2. Write the reason (the renter reads it). On a confirmed booking or a rental in progress you can type the plan''s price for this booking, for example for the days left.
3. Press the button. An offer is sent again with the new price. A confirmed booking gets the plan line and the extra is open to collect on the Money tab: Collect sends the pay link. The renter is emailed what changed.

The card coverage proof and its review task are cleared for you. **Switch to card coverage** puts them back, or gives you a task to get the proof from the renter. Sales switches requests and offers only.

## Unanswered

**More customer service** > **Unanswered**: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.', 'Customer service', 'Requests and offers, new quotes, renter messages, find a renter, owner forms, late returns.',
  'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Press **Adjust the booking** to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then **Save changes**.
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

